;
;  LOD100 overlay descriptor.
;
;  The task does not fit unaided: with every program unit carrying the
;  loader common blocks, $DATAP overflows and TKB deletes the
;  allocation.  The original had the same problem -- INSTAL.TXT 9.14
;  reproduces LOD100's own descriptor, and LNK10.CMD, by contrast, has
;  none.  This is a descriptor for the reconstruction's own module
;  decomposition, not a copy of FPS's.
;
;  The root holds the driver, the command scanner and everything more
;  than one branch calls: the symbol table, the number and name
;  packers, and the load-module word emitter.  The four branches are
;  mutually exclusive because DISPAT enters exactly one per command.
;
        .ROOT   ROOTS-LIBR-*(LOADB,OUTB,OVLB,FINB)
ROOTS:  .FCTR   LOD100/LB:LOD100:INIT:DISPAT:COMAND:FLD2:NUMIN-RS2
RS2:    .FCTR   LOD100/LB:SYMLU:PACK6:GETNUM:STARS:EMITW:EDUMP-RS3
RS3:    .FCTR   LOD100/LB:EFLUSH:PUTHDR:PUT32:OVCLOS:OVVIS
; LIB100 belongs in the root: LOAD calls INFILE, and the original ODL
; (INSTAL.TXT 9.14) likewise ends its root factor with LIB100/LB.  Without
; it TKB reports "1 UNDEFINED SYMBOLS SEGMENT LOAD" and the call lands on
; address 0 -- an odd address trap the moment a file is opened.
LIBR:   .FCTR   LB:[1,1]LIB100/LB-LB:[1,1]SYSLIB/LB
; INFILE is named explicitly here, which is how FPS's own descriptors do
; it -- ASM100's root lists LIB100/LB:DUTIL:ICMP16:... by name and DBG100
; carries a whole factor "INFIL: .FCTR LB:LIB100/LB:INFILE".  Naming the
; library alone in the root does not pull it in for a reference made from
; an overlay segment: TKB still reports 1 UNDEFINED SYMBOL SEGMENT LOAD.
LOADB:  .FCTR   LOD100/LB:LOAD:LODFIL:LOADMP-LB:[1,1]LIB100/LB:INFILE:DUTIL
OUTB:   .FCTR   LOD100/LB:OUTPUT:SETLM:SETPS:SETMD:SETMMX:SETMOD:SETRAD
OVLB:   .FCTR   LOD100/LB:TREE:OVADD:OVLY:TASKY:TSKOPS:APPRIO:CALLS:NUM2
FINB:   .FCTR   LOD100/LB:FINISH:LINKUP:WRTLM:EMITCD:WRTBR:PUTTCB:QLINK:HASRQ
        .END


